From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: sliva0 <sliva0mk@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Diameter: Add OC-Maximum-Rate from RFC 8582
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

RFC 8582 defines this AVP in the IETF space, which the dictionary has no
entry for at its code:

  OC-Maximum-Rate (670): Unsigned32, section 7.2.1

Each entry's type, enumerated values and grouped members are the
document's, from its clauses and AVP tables, and so are its M and V bits
where the document states them.

Generated by Seanchaí (integrations/wireshark/additions.py).
---
 resources/protocols/diameter/dictionary.xml | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/resources/protocols/diameter/dictionary.xml b/resources/protocols/diameter/dictionary.xml
index 56a8586..0717921 100644
--- a/resources/protocols/diameter/dictionary.xml
+++ b/resources/protocols/diameter/dictionary.xml
@@ -2809,6 +2809,9 @@
 				<gavp name="SourceID"/>
 			</grouped>
 		</avp>
+		<avp name="OC-Maximum-Rate" code="670" vendor-bit="mustnot">
+			<type type-name="Unsigned32"/>
+		</avp>
 		<avp name="OC-Sequence-Number" code="624" mandatory="may">
 			<type type-name="Unsigned64"/>
 		</avp>
